WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.370
A new student joined our class in March.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.520
Our teacher had her reading speed and

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.220
her accuracy from a short test.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.360
Which reading group should she join?

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.160
Today: how a model can sort new cases by

6
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.020
looking at the closest old ones.

7
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.860
Regression predicts a number, like a mark.

8
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.500
Classification predicts a label, like a

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.520
reading group or a type of fruit.

10
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.870
The model learns from examples

11
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.750
that already have labels.

12
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.190
Put every pupil on a scatter plot, speed

13
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.430
across and accuracy up, coloured by group.

14
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.560
Put the new pupil on it too.

15
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.600
The nearest neighbour method gives her

16
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.300
the group of the closest pupils.

17
00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.410
Here are her five nearest

18
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.750
classmates by group.

19
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.760
Three are in the blue group, and

20
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.900
one each in red and green.

21
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.540
The vote says blue.

22
00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.160
Closest means the shortest

23
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.460
distance on the chart.

24
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.790
We find it with Pythagoras: the square

25
00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.810
root of the gap in speed squared plus

26
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.730
the gap in accuracy squared.

27
00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.970
Make the two measures use

28
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.430
similar scales first.

29
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.870
The number of neighbours

30
00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.290
we ask is called k.

31
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.740
With k equal to one, a single

32
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.060
odd pupil can decide.

33
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.600
A small odd number such as three

34
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.720
or five is a good start.

35
00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.890
To choose between them, hold back some

36
00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.090
training pupils as a validation set: they

37
00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.010
pick k, and the test set stays locked

38
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:36.290
away.

39
00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:37.990
Quick check!

40
00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.650
With k equal to three, two neighbours are

41
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.310
in group A and one is in group B.

42
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.890
Which group does the model choose?

43
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.370
Group A, by two votes to one.

44
00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.820
The model simply copies the most common

45
00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.860
label among the nearest examples.

46
00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.370
That is why it is easy to

47
00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.390
explain to pupils.

48
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.350
In the app, open the

49
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.590
nearest neighbours lab.

50
00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.630
Drop a new point, change k, and watch the

51
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.130
regions of each colour grow and shrink.

52
00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:11.970
Your turn.

53
00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.180
A model chooses a reading

54
00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.640
group for a new pupil.

55
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.790
Does it predict a number or a label?

56
00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.540
A label, so it is classification.

57
00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.600
Remember: place the new case, find the

58
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.140
k nearest examples by distance, and

59
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.920
take the most common label.

60
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.940
Try it yourself: weigh some fruit at home

61
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.080
and score their colour from one to five.

62
00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.710
Then find the three nearest

63
00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.490
neighbours of a mystery fruit.
